{"condition": "R1", "run_id": "workshop_provider_smoke_update_gate-final-dev", "checkpoint": "tinker://9e65bbae-3ff8-5d90-aae2-8d0b7d62522a:train:0/sampler_weights/final", "question_id": "financebench_id_00807", "document_id": "3M_2023Q2_10Q", "split": "dev", "training_seed": 0, "sampling_seed": null, "derived": false, "evaluation_signature": "98bce4aa613cebe54699eb8cf8176ec08cc64dde874c989b7329634e05061fff", "F": 1.0, "A": 0.0, "G": 1.0, "Ret": 1.0, "correct": 0, "grounded_success": 0, "reward": 0.0, "unresolved": true, "grader_version": "workshop-rubric-v2-derived-provenance", "fabricated_citation": false, "stop_reason": "accepted_finish", "output_tokens": 2082, "total_reward": 0.0, "turns": 6, "submission": {"answer_type": "text", "value": "", "unit": "", "scale": "", "decision": "", "answer_text": "Based on 3M's Q2 FY2023 10\u2011Q filing (receipt\u202fr1, page\u202f5), the consolidated balance sheet reports:\n- Total current assets: $15,754\u202fmillion\n- Total inventories: $5,280\u202fmillion\n- Total current liabilities: $10,936\u202fmillion\n\nQuick ratio = (Current assets \u2013 Inventories) / Current liabilities = ($15,754\u202fM \u2013 $5,280\u202fM) / $10,936\u202fM \u2248 0.96.\n\nA quick ratio below 1 but close to 1 indicates that the firm can cover most of its short\u2011term obligations without relying on the sale of inventory, which is generally considered a reasonably healthy liquidity position, albeit slightly below the conventional 1.0 benchmark. The quick ratio is a relevant measure of liquidity because it assesses the ability to meet near\u2011term liabilities using the most liquid assets (cash, marketable securities, and receivables), excluding inventory which may be less readily convertible.\n\nCitations: receipt_id\u202fr1, document_id\u202f3M_2023Q2_10Q, page\u202f5.", "citations": [{"receipt_id": "r1", "document_id": "3M_2023Q2_10Q", "page": 5}], "calc_id": ""}, "latency_s": 10.907769018000181, "tool_calls": 6, "calculator_used": false, "